LeetCode 863 — All Nodes Distance K in Binary Tree
1. Problem Statement

You are given:

The root of a binary tree
A target node
An integer k

Return all nodes whose distance from the target is exactly k.

Distance means the number of edges between two nodes.

Example
        3
       / \
      5   1
     / \ / \
    6  2 0  8
      / \
     7   4

If:

target = 5
k = 2

The nodes at distance 2 are:

7, 4, 1

So:

Output = [7, 4, 1]
2. 🧠 Main Intuition

Normally, from a node in a binary tree, we can move only:

        parent
          ↑
          |
left ← node → right

But TreeNode doesn't contain a parent reference.

For example, from 5, we can directly access:

5.left
5.right

but we cannot do:

5.parent

So your first idea is:

Create a HashMap that stores each node's parent.

HashMap<TreeNode, TreeNode> map;

For example:

parent[5] = 3
parent[6] = 5
parent[2] = 5
parent[1] = 3

Now from any node, we can move in three directions:

        parent
           ↑
           |
left ←── node ──→ right



3. Logic :

The problem asks for all nodes at distance K from a target node. 
Since a binary tree normally allows movement only from parent to child, I first create a HashMap that stores the parent of every node.
Then I perform BFS starting from the target. During BFS, each node can move in three directions: left child, right child, and parent. 
I use a visited array to avoid going back and forth between a node and its parent. Since BFS processes nodes level by level, each level represents one unit of distance. 
When I reach distance K, the nodes currently in the queue are the answer.

4. Code :


class Solution {
    public List<Integer> distanceK(TreeNode root, TreeNode target, int k) {
        Queue<TreeNode> q=new LinkedList<>();
        HashMap<TreeNode,TreeNode> map=new HashMap<>();
        TreeNode[] visit=new TreeNode[501];
        q.offer(root);
        while(!q.isEmpty()){
            int size=q.size();
            for(int i=0;i<size;i++){
                TreeNode node=q.poll();
                if(node.left!=null){
                    map.put(node.left,node);
                    q.offer(node.left);
                }
                if(node.right!=null){
                    map.put(node.right,node);
                    q.offer(node.right);
                }
            }
        }
        q.offer(target);
        while(k!=0){
            int size=q.size();
            for(int i=0;i<size;i++){
                TreeNode node=q.poll();
                visit[node.val]=node;
                if(node.left!=null && visit[node.left.val]==null){
                    q.offer(node.left);
                }
                if(node.right!=null && visit[node.right.val]==null){
                    q.offer(node.right);
                }
                if(map.containsKey(node) && visit[map.get(node).val]==null){
                    q.offer(map.get(node));
                }
            }
            k--;
        }
        List<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
        while(!q.isEmpty()){
            list.add(q.poll().val);
        }
        return list;
    }
}
